# Formal PostgreSQL prerequisites

Accepted origin/main here is 4f76102ca99328e0b9063eb05b0352e62501e154:
schema 59 / 119 public tables. It has no scheduling tables.

Apply ddl/quota.sql followed by ddl/reservations.sql in one new contiguous
ARC-owned formal migration after the accepted GW-120, DAT-101 and metering
migration queue. This packet adds exactly two tables. ARC assigns the actual
next migration number and table count on its exact base. Never renumber or
edit an already accepted migration and never reuse schema-57/58 fingerprints.

scheduling_quota_policy is global: singleton, positive bigint revision and
allocation JSON. scheduling_reservations is cell-owned: exact attempt/job,
server tenant/workspace, local site/cell, normalized intent/demand, quota
revision and reserve/release times. It depends on installed workspaces with
the (tenant_id,id) key, sites/cells and local_site_id()/local_cell_id().
The exact DDL bytes and indexes are included. Add the global quota policy
table to scope enumeration and the cell-owned reservation to catalog checks.

ARC owns exact fresh and restored fingerprints, migration/readiness
admission, runtime grants and upgrade/downstream backup qualification.
The read needs SELECT on both tables; its FOR SHARE policy fence also needs
UPDATE privilege on at least one policy column under PostgreSQL SELECT rules:
https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-select.html
Preserve the Workspace/identity owner's existing row-lock privileges and the
Control role's permitted advisory lock/function calls. Grant no arbitrary
browser/database access. The same Control principal must also support the
separately authorized reserve/release and policy owner writes.

The new tests use an isolated superuser-owned fixture. They are not proof
of native serving-role grants or production migration/catalog readiness.
A missing table/grant is a storage failure, never an unconfigured/zero-capacity
success. Do not activate the public route before those prerequisites.

Borrowing DDL is separate and disabled by default. It is not needed to read
nominal hard ceilings and held reservations. Do not enable a borrowing policy
without its separate admitted schema and workload-owner integration. Do not
seed capacity or infer topology. Reconcile pre-cutover physical holds through
their owner before admission activation.
